course: dictionary
lesson: 13199
title: Fumbling: clumsy, unsure, searching
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fumbling means moving your hands in a clumsy, unsure way, as if you cannot see or feel well. «She was fumbling with the keys in the dark.» Her hands are not working neatly, and it is dark, so she cannot find the right key quickly.
explain: Fumbling can also describe searching or speaking. «He kept fumbling for the right words, so his speech sounded shaky.» The boy is nervous and unsure. In sport, a fumble means dropping a ball you should have caught.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in a meaning. Does «She was clumsy with the keys in the dark» still make sense? Yes, so clumsy and unsure is a good meaning for fumbling.
fact: Fumble is a verb: you fumble, he fumbles, she fumbled and they are fumbling.
fact: «Fumbling» can be an adjective, as in «fumbling fingers», which means clumsy fingers.
fact: «Fumbling» can mean searching awkwardly, as in «fumbling for the light switch» in the dark.
fact: In sport, «fumble» means dropping or failing to hold a ball you should have caught, especially in American football or cricket.
fact: Writers often use fumbling to show nerves or a hurry, which builds tension before something happens.
exercise: «She was fumbling with the buttons on her gloves.» What does fumbling mean here? | Sleeping deeply | Running very fast | *Using her hands in a clumsy, unsure way | Singing loudly
exercise: «He was fumbling for the light switch in the dark.» What is he doing? | *Searching awkwardly for something | Dancing | Painting a wall | Reading a map
exercise: A player drops a ball they should have caught. Which sport word fits? | fizzle | frown | flutter | *fumble
test: «His fumbling answer showed he was nervous.» What does fumbling suggest? | Shouting with joy | Being very tall | Running away | *Speaking in a nervous, unsure way
test: Every morning Ella ___ with her bag strap. Which verb form fits? | sings | jumps | sleeps | *fumbles
exam: «The nervous actor, fumbling for her words, dropped her script.» What does fumbling for her words mean? | *Searching unsurely for the right words | Reading the words very fast | Shouting the words loudly | Writing a long story
